{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 11,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.585,
            0.046,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "We Distribute, Yet Things Multiply"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.088,
            0.211,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.322,
            0.111,
            0.678,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}(60 - 5)^{2} &= 60^{2} - (60 \\times 5) - (5 \\times 60) + 5^{2} \\\\&= 3600 - 300 - 300 + 25 \\\\&= 3025.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.177,
            0.695,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "The area of the square of sidelength 55 is 3025 sq. units."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.197,
            0.846,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "We have seen what $( a ~ + ~ b ) ^ { 2 }$ gives when expanded. What is the expansion of $( a - b ) ^ { 2 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.234,
            0.485,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": "Using the distributive property,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.333,
            0.256,
            0.602,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array} { l } ( a - b ) ^ { 2 } = ( a - b ) \\times ( a - b ) \\\\ \\quad = ( a ) ^ { 2 } - b a - a b + ( b ) ^ { 2 } \\\\ \\quad = a ^ { 2 } - 2 a b + b ^ { 2 } . \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.316,
            0.849,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": "？ We can also use the expansion of $( a ~ + ~ b ) ^ { 2 }$ to find the expansion of $( a - b ) ^ { 2 }$ . Think how."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.358,
            0.395,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": "**Hint:** $( a - b ) ^ { 2 } = ( a + ( - b ) ) ^ { 2 } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.377,
            0.633,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": "We can now directly use the expansion of $( a + b ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.324,
            0.406,
            0.678,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "(a+(-b)^{2}=(a)^{2}+(-b)^{2}+2\\times(a)\\times(-b)",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.326,
            0.452,
            0.672,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": "**Identity 1B** $(a - b)^{2} = a^{2} + b^{2} - 2ab$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.492,
            0.839,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "？ Find the general expansion of $( a - { \\bar { b } } ) ^ { 2 }$ using geometry, as we did for $5 5 ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.528,
            0.752,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "？ Use the identity $( a - b ) ^ { 2 }$ to find the values of $\\mathrm{(a)}   99^{2}$ and (b) $5 8 ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.565,
            0.846,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": "？ Expand the following using both Identity 1B and by applying the distributive property (i) $( b - 6 ) ^ { 2 }$ (ii) $(-2a + 3)^{2}$ (iii) $( 7 y   -   \\frac { 3 } { 4 z } ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.646,
            0.424,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": "**Investigating Patterns**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.675,
            0.254,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": "**Pattern 1**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.699,
            0.444,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": "Look at the following pattern."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.411,
            0.721,
            0.588,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": "2 \\; ( 2 ^ { 2 } + 1 ^ { 2 } ) = 3 ^ { 2 } + 1 ^ { 2 }",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.751,
            0.588,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "2 \\; ( 3 ^ { 2 } + 1 ^ { 2 } ) = 4 ^ { 2 } + 2 ^ { 2 }",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.413,
            0.78,
            0.601,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "2 \\; ( 6 ^ { 2 } + 5 ^ { 2 } ) = 1 1 ^ { 2 } + 1 ^ { 2 }",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.81,
            0.597,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "2 \\; ( 5 ^ { 2 } + 3 ^ { 2 } ) = \\; 8 ^ { 2 } + 2 ^ { 2 } .",
          "image_source": "images/page_11_equation_22.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
